From 92145f5d13b5f925c8c03e34b3c76e6ec44f4459 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (sandbox)" <claude@sandbox.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:37:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Cohort assembly: twin endpoint for cohort_equity_review

New table cohort_review_ledger -- own vocabulary, own hash chain,
parallel to obligation_ledger. The twin never computes a cohort review
(see obligation_sweep's module docstring); it only receives what
obligation_sweep.py computed on the primary and chain-links it, same
independent-witness posture as every other record kind here.

POST /replica/{id}/cohort-reviews -- append one review, 422 on missing
required fields, 404 on an unregistered replica. Advisory-locked
append matching _append_obligation's pattern.

GET /replica/{id}/cohort-reviews -- full history, optionally filtered
by domain and/or obligation_kind, oldest first. An auditor asking
whether a cohort has ever flagged wants the whole history, not just
the latest sweep.

obligation_sweep.record_reviews() posts computed reviews through,
deliberately kept separate from sweep() itself -- computing and
recording are different steps with different failure modes, and a
caller may want to inspect reviews before deciding to record them.

Caught and fixed during this piece: an earlier edit in this branch had
silently dropped the _latest_states function signature line while
inserting _append_cohort_review next to it -- the obligations listing
endpoint was broken (NameError) until the full suite surfaced it.
Fixed; full suite re-run twice clean after.

10 new tests. Full suite 584 passed / 6 skipped, run twice back-to-back
from a clean ledger. ruff and bandit clean.
